      "proven_reason": "PROVEN 2026-08-24 after THREE stacked causes, each of which had to be removed before the next was visible. K=5, called 5/5, ZERO errored runs.\n\nTHE THREE CAUSES, in the order they surfaced:\n  1  THE SCENARIO NEVER APPROVED THE WRITE. Tier A with `approve: null`: every correct call was recorded {kind: tool_approval, pending: true, call_outcome: deferred}. `wrote 0` said nothing about the tool.\n  2  THE REFUSAL WAS H13's UNIFORM 'not found or not accessible'. The repo had already written an actionable sentence and `except LookupError: raise uniform_not_accessible()` discarded it. EndpointsOwnedNotShared now names the remedy for the one miss that has one, and only when the caller owns BOTH endpoints, so nothing is disclosed that it does not already hold.\n  3  THE RUNTIME PUT BACK THE ARGUMENT THE REMEDY SAID TO DROP. `book_id` selects between two endpoint rules, and _inject_context_ids fills any declared context id the model omits. The model followed the advice and the id was re-injected; the repeat-breaker ended the turn. Fixed with `_meta.mode_selecting_args`.\n\nFixing (2) alone would have made this look like the model ignoring advice. A remedy a refusal names has to be REACHABLE.\n\nWHAT THE MODEL ACTUALLY DOES, and it is the opposite of the reason on file since batch 19 ('it never called composition_motif_search AT ALL'): it resolves both motif NAMES to real UUIDs via that supplier, passes the correct direction, and picks `precedes` for 'coming before'. The name-repair and supplier-arming work.\n\n🔴 WHAT THE GREEN GATE DOES NOT SAY. There is no store-moved bar among the nine, so `wrote 0` fails nothing here, and the store diff is EMPTY on every run. That is not the tool failing to write - it is store_snapshot being unable to see this table. `motif_link` is keyed (id, from_motif_id, to_motif_id, kind, ord, created_at), with no book, chapter or project column, and `motif.book_id` is set ONLY for book-SHARED motifs, so a motif the caller merely owns belongs to the USER and cannot be attributed to a run by any key that file sweeps. _motif_link_counts was added and is not sufficient for this mode.\n\nSO THE WRITE IS PROVEN BY THE TOOL'S OWN RESULT, read from loreweave_chat.chat_messages.tool_calls during the run rather than from a store diff:\n    ok=true  {\"id\": \"01a030c0-7bbc-70d1-b142-ecbc86db0d8e\", \"ord\": null, \"kind\": \"precedes\", \"_meta\": {\"undo_hint\": ...}}\nwith `book_id` absent from the args on every call. A later query of motif_link returns zero rows and proves nothing either way: the fixtures are torn down after each run and the cascade removes them.\n\nThe SHIP cases (gate/absent/tenancy) were exercised earlier and are unchanged."
